  open_house_lead_handoff:        { consumers: ["ai_isa"], disposition: "handled", kind: "handoff", what: "the hot, unrepresented buyer leads from a Listing Concierge open house — handed to the AI ISA, which now PICKS THEM UP and qualifies each (consent-gated contact engagement) instead of the leads dying as a dashboard count; the seller-event → buyer-pipeline bridge" },
  stale_preapproval_reengage:     { consumers: ["ai_isa"], disposition: "handled", kind: "handoff",    what: "a pre-approval went stale (no active deal) — the Shopping Agent routes the EXPIRED case to the AI ISA for a re-qualification call, picked up via the canonical consent-gated contact engagement" },
  client_welcome_co_owned:        { consumers: [], disposition: "feed_only", kind: "update",     what: "ONE WELCOME EMAIL, TWO MANAGERS ON THE FILE. Owner ruling, verbatim: \"the welcome email is picked up by the listing concierge if it is a seller, shopping agent for a buyer, both listing concierge and shopping agent for both seller and buyer, sphere if lifetime.\" A contact_type of 'both' is the only case that names TWO managers, and `agent_client_messages.agent_kind` is a single text column (verified live — no array, no join table), so the ledger row and the governed send carry the FIRST manager (listing_concierge: a dual-sided move starts with the home they already own) and this signal is how the SECOND one picks the same welcome up. Published by lib/kernel/client-welcome.ts the moment the ledger row exists — NOT after a successful send, because a co-owner who only hears about the welcomes that went out cannot notice the ones the autonomy gate held. The route listing_concierge → shopping_agent is already a DECLARED collaboration edge (MANAGER_COLLABORATIONS.listing_demand_bridge), so nothing about the governance model is new here; what was missing was a second welcome-owner, not a second rail. FEED-ONLY ON PURPOSE, and this is the honest disposition rather than the convenient one: the welcome itself has already been authored, gated and sent under the owning manager, so there is no automated act left for the co-owner to perform — what they need is to KNOW, on the day, that this client is on their desk too. The move-up coordination that follows once there is a listing and a search to line up is `dual_transaction_timing`, which is a different question asked later" },
